turned in midlife  to his passion for learning and founded  the Chicago humanities festival an  annual civic event that offers scores of  lectures and performances all over the  city a member of the class of nineteen  sixty-nine took up photography more than  25 years after graduating and he has  since published an extraordinary series  of books with the National Geographic  Society and a commodities trader from  the class of 1973 recently created a  brilliant tony-nominated Broadway  musical based on the life and work of a  great Nigerian musician singer and  songwriter and there are many more such  stories important as it is for you to  fulfill your personal admiration your  personal aspirations we truly hope you  will do this but there is also more  expected of you monday at commencement  exercises Dean Miller will ask me to  confer upon you  the degrees in Yale College that you  have earned in the curious tradition of  Yale College you will then inexplicably  cheer wildly and exuberantly even though  the Dean has only asked a question and  you have not yet graduated after you  settle down I will in fact confer upon  you your degrees but what I will say to  you differs significantly from what  college presidents all around the  country will be saying to their  graduates at many schools students are  awarded the rights and privileges of  their degrees not so at Yale here your  degrees will be conferred upon you and  you will be admitted to their rights and  responsibilities the rights are simple  enough you will be entitled to have an  alumni email address forever  you'll be entitled to vote in elections  for fellows of the Yale corporation  beginning five years from now you'll be  entitled to participate in a wide  variety of alumni events and interest  groups and to receive frequent  solicitations to support your alma mater  the rights conferred by other  institutions are much the same as yours  but what is distinctive about Yale is  that we do not confer upon you  privileges but admit you to  responsibilities now you've been here  for four years and I think you know what  I'm talking about for four years you  have been free to explore as you wish  but you have also been part of a  community you have learned not simply to  excel as individuals but also to support  and encourage one another to work in  organizations to accomplish common  purposes and to help those in need  through voluntary service the  citizenship and service that you have  modeled here at Yale has prepared you  for your lifelong responsibilities  whether working in community soup  kitchens or working at the highest  levels of government whether your  contributions are part-time or voluntary  our time and voluntary or at the core of  your chosen vocations you can make a  difference in the lives of others and  history gives me confidence that you  will all around this country Yale  graduates serve disproportionately on  the boards of local charities hospitals  civic and arts organizations Yale  graduates lead most of the major  environmental organization  in the United States and 9 of 100 US  senators and three of the last four  presidents of the United States of Yale  degrees the Yale tradition of service  and leadership is one of which we are  justly proud it is your responsibility  to maintain it women and men of the  class of 2011  today we celebrate your amazing  accomplishments and we rejoice in  contemplating your enormous potential  take the time to find your passion  choose a life's work that you love and  remember that the world is now your  community serve it well congratulations
 

